								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg8240#msg8240"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg8240#msg8240">Re: Rant re Ialin on Hegemony Raid</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #30 on:</b> June 04, 2004, 12:25:51 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Perhaps he was never in the actual chat?&nbsp; Over the past couple months Ive been on several raids with other guilds doing PoP with them! </div><br />Yeah, I had that experience awhile ago too.&nbsp; I&#039;m not sure what the logic was.&nbsp; I was a guest on a raid.&nbsp; I two box a warrior and a cleric.&nbsp; I asked if there were tank and/or healer channels I needed to know about and was told that there were such channels, but I wasn&#039;t allowed to be in them.&nbsp; &nbsp;Errrr.... ok. So... you don&#039;t want the people coming along on your raid to know what&#039;s going on?&nbsp; Sweet.&nbsp; heh... at least information was given in /rs and I&#039;d done the raid targets before.<br /><br />So I guess it depends on where instructions were given.&nbsp; The implication is that most everything was stated in /rs or some other channel that the guest had access too.<br /><br />Whatever... I&#039;m just bored.&nbsp; Someone flame more or something.<br /><br />&nbsp;
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
